    "roles": ["band_member", "touring", "composer"],
    "summary": "Siouxsie and the Banshees' drummer from 1979 to their split in 1996, and Siouxsie's partner in the Creatures. From Liverpool's punk scene and the Slits' Cut, he joined the Banshees as a stand-in for Kenny Morris and stayed. He moved the groove off the hi-hat and onto the toms: the floor tom in eighths or sixteenths, four on the floor beneath it, the snare kept for 2 and 4 or every beat, and sometimes no snare or no bass drum at all. Spin: 'he didn't just play rhythms - he played hooks and leads'; Stewart Copeland: 'a lot of tom-toms and a big throb'."
  },
